.DS_Store
.idea
.idea/*
CLAUDE.md

# Oversized aggregate exports are generated and verified on every harvest,
# then published as immutable assets on the release keyed to the data commit.
# GitHub rejects these individual files above its 100 MiB push limit. Keep
# other source exports and individual records tracked; do not ignore the tree.
api/v1/all.jsonld
api/v1/all.ttl
api/v1/sources/ru.jsonld
api/v1/sources/ru.ttl

# The catalogue lists the files present on disk when the export finishes
# (manifest_datasets keeps only paths that File.exist?), so here it would
# advertise the aggregate files above even though the tracked tree omits them.
# It has never been committed: the last publish predates the catalogue.
# Ignored rather than post-processed, because a hand-edited catalogue claiming
# to be the exporter's output is worse than no catalogue. The cost is that
# this tree carries no root discovery document for the collections it does
# publish, until the exporter can describe a published subset.
api/v1/index.jsonld
